# Operator Hierarchy and Permissions

## Depth and parent rules

- Operators spawned by other operators default to **readonly** preset.
- Children cannot exceed parent preset — cascade applies at spawn time.
- Cascade dismiss: when an operator is dismissed, all its children are also dismissed.
- Use `checkPermissionForOperator()` for operator-aware permission checks (not name-based `checkPermission()`).

## Permission presets

| Preset | Capabilities |
|--------|--------------|
| readonly | fileRead, gitRead, modelCall |
| standard | + fileWrite, terminalExecute, gitWrite |
| full | + webSearch |

## Implementation

- `operatorRegistry.spawn()` accepts `parentId` and `preset`; child preset is capped by parent.
- `toolAllowlist.checkPermissionForOperator(op, capability)` uses effective preset (registry + config overrides).
- Config overrides (`cursorDrive.agents.permissions.overrides`) can only restrict, never grant beyond registry preset.
